&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A primary risk assessment based on integration of clinical evaluation and non-molecular&sol;non-proteomic laboratory testing, [e.g., fibrosis-4 index (FIB-4) &amp;#8805; 1.3], as outlined by consensus guidelines, does not indicate low risk.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Liver stiffness measurement (LSM) by imaging [e.g., vibration controlled transient elastography (VCTE), magnetic resonance elastography (MRE)] has not been performed within the prior 12 months or results were indeterminate.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The results of the test will be used to directly aid in pending management decisions (e.g., referral to a specialist, performance of liver biopsy, eligibility for &sol; monitoring of pharmacologic therapy) as documented in the patient&amp;#8217;s medical record.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Testing is not performed more than once within a 12-month period nor within 12 months following a liver biopsy with definitive histologic interpretation by a pathologist.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test has satisfactorily completed a Technical Assessment (TA) by the Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;).&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Clinical validity (CV) of any novel analytes must be established through a study published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population with comparability across subgroups.&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the test relies on an algorithm, the algorithm must be validated in a cohort that is not a development cohort for the algorithm.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test must demonstrate equivalent or superior performance to analytes already covered under this policy for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Molecular and proteomic tests utilizing a similar methodology or evaluating similar analytes as a test for which existing coverage has been established must demonstrate equivalent or superior test performance when used for the same indication in the same intended use population.&amp;#160;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

