&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-03, Medicare National Coverage Determinations (NCD) Manual, Chapter 1, Part 4, &amp;#167;270.3 Blood-Derived Products for Chronic Non-Healing Wounds&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This is a NON-coverage Local Coverage Determination (LCD) for irreversible electroporation (IRE) as a means of managing cancer except as follows:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Favorable, Intermediate Risk Prostate Cancer, Grade Group 2&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Intermediate-risk prostate cancer, Grade Group 2, coverage may be considered reasonable and necessary if &lt;strong&gt;all&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Face to face discussion with the patient regarding risks of treatment with IRE versus other treatment options is documented.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Options discussed should include active surveillance, radiation therapy, and radical prostatectomy.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Providers should inform patients with intermediate risk prostate cancer considering whole gland or focal ablation that there is a lack of high-quality data comparing ablation outcomes to radiation therapy, surgery and active surveillance.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patients have not been previously treated with IRE.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patient counselling shall include: &lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;IRE is not U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved or cleared for the treatment of prostate cancer&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Biopsy-detected cancer after focal therapy (FT) is common within 2 years post-treatment&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;FT or whole gland ablative therapy may impact the safety and&sol;or efficacy of subsequent local therapy&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patients considering ablation should be counseled regarding side effects and recurrence risk and should be followed post-ablation with prostate surface antigen (PSA), digital rectal exam (DRE), magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), and biopsy tailored to their specific health and cancer characteristics.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Metastatic Colorectal Cancer to Liver&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Metastatic colorectal cancer treatment with IRE to the liver may be considered reasonable and necessary if &lt;strong&gt;all&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patients that cannot be safely resected or ablated with margins due to proximity to central bile ducts or other structures that cannot be protected, IRE may be considered.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Face-to-face discussion with patients regarding risks of treatment with IRE versus other treatment options is documented.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Options discussed should include alternative treatment options and medical necessity of IRE over either radiofrequency ablation (RFA) or surgical excision.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Providers should inform patients that there is a lack of high-quality data to support this treatment option.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patients should not have had previous failed IRE at the site to be treated as the incidence of higher adverse events (AEs) is unknown.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Patient counselling shall include that IRE is not FDA cleared or approved for the treatment of liver cancer.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A), states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;42 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) &amp;sect;410.32 Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;This contractor will cover molecular diagnostic tests for use in a beneficiary with bladder cancer when all of the following conditions are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The beneficiary is being actively managed for bladder cancer.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The beneficiary is within the population and has the indication for which the test was developed and is covered. The laboratory will make available the appropriate indications of the test to the treating&sol;ordering physician.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 1 of the 2 criteria are met:
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient is a candidate for multiple potential treatments, which could be considered to have varied or increasing levels of intensity based on a consensus guideline, and the physician and patient must decide among these treatments. &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;OR&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient is a candidate for multiple therapies, and the test has shown that it predicts response to a specific therapy among accepted therapy options based on nationally recognized society consensus guidelines (i.e., National Comprehensive Cancer Network [NCCN], American Society of Clinical Oncology [ASCO], Society of Urologic Oncology [SUO], or American Urological Association [AUA]).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) methodology is used in testing, the conditions set by NCD 90.2 are fulfilled (summarized: the patient has advanced cancer; plans on being treated for said cancer, and has not been previously tested with the same test for the same genetic content)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test demonstrates analytical validity including both analytical and clinical validations. If the test relies on an algorithm (which may range in complexity from a threshold determination of a single numeric value to a complex mathematical or computational function), the algorithm must be validated in a cohort that is not a development cohort for the algorithm.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test has demonstrated clinical validity and utility, establishing a clear and significant biological&sol;molecular basis for stratifying patients and subsequently selecting (either positively or negatively) a clinical management decision (in 4. above) in a clearly defined population.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test successfully completes a Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) technical assessment that ensures the test is reasonable and necessary as described above.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Only 1 test may be performed prior to the initiation of therapy UNLESS a second test that interrogates different genomic content AND meets all the criteria established herein, is reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: circle;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The genomic content interrogated by the test must be relevant to the therapy under consideration.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

