indication:
&lt;p&gt;This Medicare contractor will provide limited coverage for the Breast Cancer Index&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; (BCI) gene expression test (Biotheranostics, Inc., San Diego, CA). The BCI test is used by physicians to provide a genomic-based estimate of distant recurrence risk when considering addition of chemotherapy, and&sol;or late distant recurrence risk and endocrine responsiveness when considering extension of endocrine therapy, depending upon when in the continuum of care testing is requested.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The BCI test is covered for postmenopausal women with invasive breast cancer when the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pathology reveals invasive carcinoma of the breast that is estrogen-receptor positive (ER+) and&sol;or progesterone receptor positive (PR+) and Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2 negative (HER2-); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient has early-stage disease {Tumor, Node, Metastasis (TNM) stage T1-3, pN0-N1, M0}; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient has no evidence of distant breast cancer metastasis (i.eg., non-relapsed); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test results will be used in determining treatment management of the patient for chemotherapy and&sol;or endocrine therapy.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

