&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;#167;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;#167;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;#167;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;#167;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Indications and Limitations of Coverage&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This policy provides limited coverage for multi-gene &lt;strong&gt;non-next generation sequencing (NGS)&lt;&sol;strong&gt; panel testing and limited coverage for single-gene testing for the diagnostic workup of patients with suspected &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; negative myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs). &lt;em&gt;Classical&lt;&sol;em&gt; &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; negative MPNs include Polycythemia Vera (PV), Essential Thrombocythemia (ET) and Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF), and &lt;em&gt;non-classical&lt;&sol;em&gt; &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; negative MPNs include Chronic Neutrophilic Leukemia (CNL) and Chronic Eosinophilic Leukemia, Not Otherwise Specified (CEL, NOS), among other rare entities. Myelodysplastic&sol;Myeloproliferative neoplasms are considered a separate class outside the scope of this LCD.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Testing myeloid and suspected neoplasms by NGS is covered by a separate LCD&lt;em&gt;, MolDX: Next-Generation Sequencing Lab-Developed Tests for Myeloid Malignancies and Suspected Myeloid Malignancies (L38123).&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;ALL of the following criteria must be met:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;1. The patient is being evaluated for a &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt;-negative MPN according to national or international consensus diagnostic criteria (i.e., World Health Organization (WHO); International Consensus Classification (ICC)).&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;2. Testing follows the assessment of &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; (this is required unless the patient is only suspected of having PV). &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;3. The test is comprised of one or more highly sensitive single- or multi- gene assays (i.e. quantitative polymerase chain reaction [PCR], digital droplet PCR [ddPCR]) that can accurately detect a minimum variant allele frequency (VAF) of &amp;#8804;1% for &lt;em&gt;JAK2&lt;&sol;em&gt; (and 1-3% for&lt;em&gt; CALR&lt;&sol;em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MPL&lt;&sol;em&gt; when they are included in the testing).&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;4. &lt;&sol;span&gt;If testing is performed using single gene tests, a sequential and reflexive approach is expected. Once a positive result is obtained and the appropriate diagnosis is established, further testing should stop unless required for subsequent management of the patient or as further described below.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;When testing for the &lt;em&gt;classical&lt;&sol;em&gt; &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt;-negative MPNs (PV, ET, or PMF) &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;using single gene tests&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;, reflex testing to the next gene will be considered reasonable and necessary according to the following sequence of tests for known driver mutations:&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; negative test results, progress to ii. &lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Note: For the rare patient with high clinical suspicion of PV despite a positive &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; result, testing for a mutation in &lt;em&gt;JAK2&lt;&sol;em&gt; mutation may still be performed. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;JAK2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;V617F negative test results (this includes &lt;em&gt;JAK2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;V617F positive at &amp;lt;1% VAF), progress to iii or iv.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;JAK2&lt;&sol;em&gt;, exon 12 (required when PV is suspected)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Calreticulin (&lt;em&gt;CALR&lt;&sol;em&gt;) and Thrombopoietin Receptor (&lt;em&gt;MPL&lt;&sol;em&gt;) driver mutations (required when ET or PMF is suspected)&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Note: testing for &lt;em&gt;CALR&sol;MPL&lt;&sol;em&gt; does NOT require a negative &lt;em&gt;JAK2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;exon 12, just a negative &lt;em&gt;JAK2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;V617F result.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;5. If testing is performed using a panel (i.e., multiplex PCR) the panel must include at least the minimum necessary genes and gene alterations that would be reasonably expected by the test to achieve a diagnosis according to national or international consensus guidelines, given the specific MPN subtype suspected. For example:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Molecular testing for mutations in &lt;em&gt;JAK-2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;(including V617F and exon 12), &lt;em&gt;CALR &lt;&sol;em&gt;and &lt;em&gt;MPL &lt;&sol;em&gt;genes is considered medically necessary for the identification of the classical MPNs.&amp;#160;&lt;br &sol;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot; type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;However, if the accelerated&sol;blast phase of PMF is suspected at diagnosis, molecular testing should also include acute myeloid leukemia (AML)- associated mutations and would likely require the performance of a NGS panel; in this case, a panel that does not include the AML-associated mutations does not meet the minimum necessary gene requirements.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Additional&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; MPN-associated genes must also be included as appropriate for the identification of other &lt;em&gt;non-classical&lt;&sol;em&gt; &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt;-negative MPNs. For example, when CNL is suspected, testing for the colony stimulating factor 3 receptor (&lt;em&gt;CSF3R&lt;&sol;em&gt;) is required. Note also that testing for CNL requires the exclusion of the classical &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt;-negative MPNs.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;6. Patients with high suspicion of a &lt;em&gt;BCR-ABL&lt;&sol;em&gt; negative MPN who test negative by a &lt;u&gt;non-NGS&lt;&sol;u&gt; test for mutations in &lt;em&gt;JAK2 &lt;&sol;em&gt;(including the detection of &lt;em&gt;JAK2&lt;&sol;em&gt; V617F at a VAF &amp;lt;1%), &lt;em&gt;CALR&lt;&sol;em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;MPL &lt;&sol;em&gt;and&sol;or &lt;em&gt;CSF3R &lt;&sol;em&gt;may have a subsequent NGS panel performed for additional relevant mutations, as outlined in national or international consensus guidelines. The additional testing by NGS must comprise non-duplicative genetic alterations.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;7. Clinical validity (CV) of analytes measured must be established through a study published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;8. The test is being used (a) in a patient who is part of the population in which the test was analytically validated and (b) according to the intended use of the test.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;9. &lt;&sol;span&gt;The test satisfactorily completes a technical assessment (TA) that will evaluate and confirm that analytical validity (AV), clinical validity (CV), and clinical utility (CU) have been demonstrated.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;10. Tests utilizing a similar methodology or evaluating a similar molecular analyte to a test for which there is a generally accepted testing standard or for which existing coverage exists must demonstrate equivalent or superior test performance (i.e., sensitivity and&sol;or specificity) when used for the same indication in the intended-use population.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;11. Testing is performed for diagnosis and not as a test of cure or for monitoring minimal residual disease (MRD).&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;NOTE: Testing by NGS falls outside of the scope of this LCD but must fulfill the criteria outlined in LCD &lt;em&gt;L38123&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;, MolDX: Next-Generation Sequencing Lab-Developed Tests for Myeloid Malignancies and Suspected Myeloid Malignancies.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A)&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 123%;&quot;&gt;allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(D) Allows coverage and payment for clinical care items and services provided with the concurrence of the Secretary and with respect to research and experimentation conducted by, or under contract with, the Medicare Payment Advisory Commission or the Secretary, which are not reasonable and necessary to carry out the purposes of section&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;42 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) 410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes, &amp;sect;80.6 Requirements for Ordering and Following Orders for Diagnostic Tests&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;42 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) 410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet Only Manuals, Pub 100-02 Medicare Beneficiary Policy Manual Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left; color: #212529; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; font-family: Verdana, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; word-spacing: 0px; float: none; display: inline !important; white-space: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: #ffffff; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; text-decoration-thickness: initial;&quot;&gt; &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;This is a limited coverage policy for assays that detect biomarkers from circulating tumor cells (CTCs).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Criteria for Coverage&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cancers with established biomarker testing, as recommended by society or national guidelines&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Assays that detect biomarkers from CTCs are covered when ALL of the following are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The patient has been diagnosed with cancer&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The specific cancer type has an associated biomarker&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The associated biomarker has already established clinical utility (CU) in the peer-reviewed published literature for the intended cancer type and for the specific indication in the intended patient population&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The biomarker&amp;rsquo;s CU may include any of the following: it can be used to diagnose, risk-stratify, predict, or monitor response to therapy, as recommended by national or society guidelines (i.e., American Society of Clinical Oncology (ASCO), National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN))&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least 1 of the following criteria are met AND there is clear documentation of at least 1 of these in the medical record:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The patient&amp;rsquo;s cancer has not previously been tested for the specific biomarker, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The patient has newly metastatic cancer, and a metastatic lesion has not been tested for the specific biomarker, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The patient demonstrates signs of clinical, radiological or pathologic disease progression, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is concern for resistance to treatment based on specific and well-established clinical indications&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testing for the biomarker can be performed using CTCs&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CTC-based biomarker test successfully completes a comprehensive Technical Assessment (TA) by Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&amp;reg;) that will ensure that Analytical Validity (AV) (including an analytical and clinical validation), Clinical Validity (CV), and CU criteria are met to establish the test as Reasonable and Necessary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The clinical validation has demonstrated performance that is equivalent or superior to tissue-based testing or another already-accepted test for the same biomarker for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CV (for new analytes) must be established through studies published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tissue-based testing for the specific biomarker is infeasible (e.g., quantity not sufficient or invasive biopsy is medically contraindicated) &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt; will not provide sufficient information for subsequent medical management (e.g., in cases where human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2) overexpression is negative in a tissue biopsy but may be positive in the CTCs, due to tumor heterogeneity). There is clear documentation of at least 1 of these reasons for testing in the medical record.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a given patient encounter, only 1 test for assessing the biomarker may be performed UNLESS a second test, meeting all the criteria established herein, is reasonable and necessary as an adjunct to the first test.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Duplicate testing of the same biomarker (&lt;em&gt;from the same sample type and for the same clinical indication&lt;&sol;em&gt;) using different methodologies is not covered. For example, testing for androgen receptor splice variant 7 (AR-V7) from CTCs by messenger RNA (mRNA) as well as &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;immunohistochemistry&lt;&sol;span&gt; (IHC)-based methodologies, for the same clinical indication, will not be covered.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;#167;1862(a)(1)(A). Allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis and treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;42 CFR &amp;#167;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;#167;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;#167;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;p&gt;
