&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;&amp;sect;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 122%;&quot;&gt;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 16, &amp;sect;50.5 Jurisdiction of Laboratory Claims, &amp;sect;60.1.1 Independent Laboratory Specimen Drawing, &amp;sect;60.2 Travel Allowance&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Molecular diagnostic tests used to assist in risk stratification of melanoma patients are covered when ALL of the following are true:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The patient has a personal history of melanoma AND:&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Either: &lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Has Stage T1b and above OR&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Has T1a with documented concern about adequacy of microstaging&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Is undergoing workup or being evaluated for treatment, AND&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Does not have metastatic disease AND&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Presumed risk for a positive Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy (SLNB) based on clinical, histological, or other information is &amp;gt;5% AND&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Has a disease stage, grade, and Breslow thickness (or other qualifying conditions) within the intended use of the test&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The TEST has demonstrated, as part of a Technical Assessment:&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Clinical validity of analytes tested in predicting metastatic disease (or the absence of metastatic disease) in peer-reviewed scientific literature &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Utility beyond clinical, histological, and radiographical factors in the ability to accurately stratify patients into risk groups to manage patient care, such by precluding unnecessary sentinel lymph node biopsies&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Appropriate analytical validity&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Performance characteristics equivalent or superior to other covered, similar tests&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left; color: #212529; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; font-family: Verdana, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; box-sizing: border-box; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: #ffffff; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left; color: #212529; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; font-family: Verdana, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; box-sizing: border-box; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: #ffffff; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32 Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left; color: #212529; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; font-family: Verdana, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; box-sizing: border-box; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: #ffffff; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Change&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Indications and Limitations of Coverage&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;This policy provides limited coverage for methylation analysis for hypermethylation of the O-6-&amp;shy;methylguanine DNA methyltransferase (MGMT) gene promoter. MGMT methylation analysis testing is considered to be reasonable and necessary for adult patients when the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tumor type is high&amp;shy;-grade malignant glioma (e.g. glioblastoma multiforme (GBM), anaplastic astrocytoma) &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt; &lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patients are able to tolerate temozolomide therapy or radiation therapy, and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The physician will use the MGMT testing results to decide between radiation therapy and chemotherapy alone as 1st line adjuvant treatment, or between temozolomide and other chemotherapy for 1st line adjuvant treatment&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: This assessment is predicated on the assumption that therapy is considered beneficial for the specific patient.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The purpose of this test is to assist dermatopathologists to arrive at the correct diagnosis of melanoma versus non-melanoma when examining skin biopsies.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;This Medicare contractor will provide limited coverage for molecular&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA)&sol;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;Ribonucleic acid &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;(RNA) assays that aid in the diagnosis or exclusion of melanoma from a biopsy when ALL of the following clinical conditions are met:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test is ordered by a board-certified or board-eligible dermatopathologist &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The specimen is a primary (non-metastatic, non-re-excision specimen) cutaneous melanocytic neoplasm for which the diagnosis is equivocal&sol;uncertain (i.e., clear distinction between benign or malignant cannot be achieved using clinical and&sol;or histopathological features alone) despite the performance of standard-of-care test procedures and relevant ancillary tests (i.e., immunohistochemical stains) &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The specimen includes an area representative of the lesion or portion of the lesion that is suspicious for malignancy&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The patient may be subjected to additional intervention, such as re-excision and&sol;or sentinel lymph node biopsy, as a result of the diagnostic uncertainty&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The patient has not been tested with the same or similar assay for the same clinical lesion&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 121%;&quot;&gt;The test is validated for use in the intended-use population and is performed according to its stated intended-use &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test demonstrates Analytical and Clinical Validity (AV and CV) and Clinical Utility (CU) and undergoes a technical assessment (TA) by MolDX&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&amp;#174; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;to demonstrate compliance of the service with this policy&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Tests that demonstrate similar indicated uses and equivalent or superior performance to covered tests may similarly be covered under this policy.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

