indication:
&lt;p&gt;This is a laboratory test which will assist physicians caring for patients who have developed pulmonary (lung) scarring.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This policy provides limited coverage for the Envisia&amp;trade; Genomic Classifier (Veracyte&amp;trade;, Inc., South San Francisco, CA), a tissue based multi-analyte assay with algorithm analysis test (hereafter called Envisia&amp;trade;) for interstitial lung disease (ILD) patients who are suspected of having idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF) and who do not have a definitive usual interstitial pneumonia (UIP) pattern by high resolution computed tomography (HRCT) or other known cause of ILD. IPF suspicion increases significantly in patients greater than 60 years of age when HRCT is not definitive, and comorbidities in this population make clinicians reluctant to perform surgical lung biopsy to obtain a diagnosis due to significant procedure morbidity and mortality. Envisia&amp;trade; testing is performed on less-invasive bronchoscopy transbronchial biopsy (TBB) samples and is intended to provide a categorical UIP or non-UIP result that along with clinical and radiographic information may guide treatment without the need or risk of surgical lung biopsy.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This is a coverage policy for gene expression profile tests that assess risk or predict therapeutic response in men who have an established diagnosis of castration resistant or metastatic prostate cancer. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Such testing is considered reasonable and necessary to help guide treatment decisions in men with prostate cancer and a life expectancy such that they are candidates for prostate cancer treatment according to the most recent nationally recognized guidelines at the time of testing or based on FDA labelling of drugs and biologics available as potential treatment options.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The scope of this policy includes gene expression profile tests regardless of methodology. It is exclusive of targeted and comprehensive genomic profiles (CGP) by next generation sequencing (NGS) and single biomarker expression analyses. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Coverage criteria:&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. BOTH of the following criteria must be met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The beneficiary is being actively managed for castration resistant or metastatic (hormone sensitive or castration resistant) prostate cancer.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The beneficiary is within the population and has the indication for which the test was developed and validated.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. At least 1 of the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The patient is a candidate for more than one management option, which could be considered to have varied, or increasing&sol;decreasing levels of intensity based on a nationally recognized consensus guideline, and the physician and patient must decide among these treatments OR&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The patient is a candidate for more than one management option, and the test has shown that it predicts response to a specific therapy among accepted therapy options based on nationally recognized consensus guidelines and&sol;or FDA labelling.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;3. The patient has not been tested with the same or similar test for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;4. The patient has not received pelvic radiation or androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) prior to the biopsy or prostate resection specimen on which the test will be performed. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The only exception to this is for men who are na&amp;iuml;ve to secondary systemic therapies (that could be given after ADT monotherapy) AND at least 1 of the following is true:&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;a. They do not have other standard-of-care drug-targetable gene alterations to guide systemic therapy, as defined in nationally recognized guidelines OR&lt;br &sol;&gt;b. They have other standard-of-care drug-targetable gene alterations to guide systemic therapy, as defined in nationally recognized guidelines but they are not eligible for those therapies for another reason.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; The test demonstrates analytical validity (AV), clinical validity (CV) and clinical utility (CU), establishing a clear and significant biological&sol; molecular basis for stratifying patients and subsequently selecting (either positively or negatively) a clinical management in a clearly defined population.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;6&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; Clinical validity of any analytes (or expression profiles) measured must be established through a study published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;7&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; If the test relies on an algorithm, the algorithm must be validated in a cohort that is not a development cohort for the algorithm.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;8&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; Testing must be performed according to Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA) and&sol;or Food and Drug Administration (FDA) regulations in an accredited laboratory.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;9&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; The lab providing the test is responsible for clearly indicating to treating physicians the population and indication(s) for test use.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;10&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; The test successfully completes a Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) Technical Assessment that ensures that AV, CV, and CU criteria set in this policy are met to establish the test as Reasonable and Necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Genomic expression profile tests that demonstrate equivalent or superior analytical and clinical validity to those covered by this contractor will be considered reasonable and necessary for the same indications. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
