&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A), states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that &amp;ldquo;are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&amp;rdquo;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
