&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act section 1862(a)(10). This section excludes cosmetic surgery, except as required to repair an accidental injury or for improvement of the function of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act section 1833 (e). This section prohibits Medicare payment for any claim which lacks the necessary information to process the claim.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Pub 100-02 &lt;em&gt;Medicare Benefit Policy Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Chapter 16 &amp;#8211; General Exclusion from Coverage, Section 20 &amp;#8211; Services Not Reasonable and Necessary and Section 120 &amp;#8211; Cosmetic Surgery.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
