indication:
&lt;p&gt;This test is a &amp;#8220;liquid biopsy&amp;#8221;. It is intended to assist physicians caring for patients who suffer from a common form of lung cancer and who have advanced disease.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This policy provides limited coverage for InvisionFirst&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; - Lung (Inivata&amp;#8482;, Research Triangle Park, NC) (hereafter InVision&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) a plasma-based, somatic comprehensive genomic profiling (CGP) test for patients with advanced (Stage IIIB&sol;IV) non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At diagnosis&lt;&sol;strong&gt; &amp;#8211;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When results for EGFR single nucleotide variants (SNVs) and insertions and deletions (indels); rearrangements in ALK and ROS1; and SNVs for BRAF are not available AND when tissue-based CGP is infeasible [i.e., quantity not sufficient (QNS) for tissue-based CGP or invasive biopsy is medically contraindicated],
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At progression&lt;&sol;strong&gt; &amp;#8211;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For patients progressing on or after chemotherapy or immunotherapy who have not been tested for EGFR SNVs and indels; rearrangements in ALK and ROS1; and SNVs for BRAFs, and for whom tissue-based CGP is infeasible;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For patients progressing on EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs),&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If no genetic alteration is detected by InVision&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#174;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; or if circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) is insufficient&sol;not detected, tissue-based genotyping should be considered.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

