&lt;p&gt;CMS Transmittal No. 423, Publication 100-04, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Change Request #3632, January 6, 2005. Update of the Hospital Outpatient Prospective Payment, includes Kyphoplasty.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;PVA (percutaneous vertebroplasty (PVP) or percutaneous kyphoplasty (PKP)) is covered in patients who qualify based on the following criteria:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Inclusion criteria (&lt;strong&gt;ALL are required&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute (&amp;lt;6 weeks) or subacute (6-12 weeks) osteoporotic VCF (T1 &amp;#8211; L5) by recent (within 30 days) advanced imaging (bone marrow edema on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) or bone-scan&sol;single photon emission computed tomography (SPECT)&sol;computed tomography (CT) uptake)&lt;sup&gt;1-3,10,25,27&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Symptomatic (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hospitalized with severe pain (Numeric Rating Scale (NRS) or Visual Analog Scale (VAS) pain score &amp;#8805;8)&lt;sup&gt;4-7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-hospitalized with moderate-to-severe pain (NRS or VAS &amp;#8805;5) despite optimal non-surgical management (NSM)&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;* (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worsening pain&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stable-to-improved pain (but NRS or VAS still &amp;#8805;5) (&lt;strong&gt;with &amp;#8805; 2 of the following&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: upper-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progression of vertebral body height loss&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;gt;25% vertebral body height reduction&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kyphotic deformity&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Severe impact of VCF on daily functioning (Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire (RDQ) &amp;gt;17)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 240px;&quot;&gt;*Consider including pedicle periosteal infiltration&lt;sup&gt;7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;c. Continuum of care&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(BOTH)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All patients presenting with VCF should be referred for evaluation of bone mineral density (BMD) and osteoporosis education for subsequent treatment as indicated.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All patients with VCF should be instructed to take part in an osteoporosis prevention&sol;treatment program.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Exclusion criteria&lt;sup&gt;2,5,8-10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;a. Absolute contraindication:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current back pain is not primarily due to the identified acute or subacute VCF(s)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Osteomyelitis, discitis or active systemic or surgical site infection&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pregnancy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;b. Relative contraindication:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Allergy to bone cement or opacification agents&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Uncorrected coagulopathy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Spinal instability&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Myelopathy from the fracture&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Neurologic deficit&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Neural impingement&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Fracture retropulsion&sol;canal compromise&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Greater than 3 vertebral fractures&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vertebral augmentation and kyphoplasty for VCFs with intractable spinal pain not relieved with medical therapy will be covered for osteolytic vertebral metastatic disease or myeloma involving a vertebral body.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: Verdana,&amp;amp;quot; helvetica neue&amp;amp;quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-top: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: inline !important; float: none; background-color: #ffffff; color: #212529; font-family: Verdana,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: Verdana,&amp;amp;quot; helvetica neue&amp;amp;quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-top: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Ordering diagnostic tests&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot; &sol;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot; &sol;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;411.15(k)(1) Particular services excluded from coverage&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;PVA (percutaneous vertebroplasty (PVP) or percutaneous kyphoplasty (PKP)) is covered in patients who qualify based on the following criteria&lt;&sol;span&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Inclusion criteria (&lt;strong&gt;ALL are required&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):&amp;#160;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute (&amp;lt;6 weeks) or subacute (6-12 weeks) osteoporotic VCF (T1 &amp;#8211; L5) by recent (within 30 days) advanced imaging (bone marrow edema on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) or bone-scan&sol;single photon emission computed tomography (SPECT)&sol;computed tomography (CT) uptake)&lt;sup&gt;1-3,10,25,27&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Symptomatic (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hospitalized with severe pain (Numeric Rating Scale (NRS) or Visual Analog Scale (VAS) pain score &amp;#8805;8)&lt;sup&gt;4-7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-hospitalized with moderate-to-severe pain (NRS or VAS &amp;#8805;5) despite optimal non-surgical management (NSM)&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;* (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worsening pain&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stable-to-improved pain (but NRS or VAS still &amp;#8805;5) (&lt;strong&gt;with &amp;#8805; 2 of the following&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: upper-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progression of vertebral body height loss&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;&amp;gt;25% vertebral body height reduction&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Kyphotic deformity&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Severe impact of VCF on daily functioning (Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire (RDQ) &amp;gt;17)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 160px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;*Consider including pedicle periosteal infiltration&lt;sup&gt;7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;c. &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Continuum of care&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(BOTH)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All patients presenting with VCF should be referred for evaluation of bone mineral density (BMD) and osteoporosis education for subsequent treatment as indicated.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All patients with VCF should be instructed to take part in an osteoporosis prevention&sol;treatment program.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Exclusion criteria&lt;sup&gt;2,5,8-10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;a. &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Absolute contraindication:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Current back pain is not primarily due to the identified acute or subacute VCF(s)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Osteomyelitis, discitis or active systemic or surgical site infection&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pregnancy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;b. Relative contraindication:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allergy to bone cement or opacification agents&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncorrected coagulopathy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spinal instability&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Myelopathy from the fracture&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Neurologic deficit&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Neural impingement&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fracture retropulsion&sol;canal compromise&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Greater than 3 vertebral fractures&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Vertebral augmentation and kyphoplasty for VCFs with intractable spinal pain not relieved with medical therapy will be covered for osteolytic vertebral metastatic disease or myeloma involving a vertebral body.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

