&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that &amp;ldquo;are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&amp;rdquo;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt; background: white;&quot;&gt;42 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) &amp;sect;410.32 Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt; background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS IOM Publication 100-03, &lt;em&gt;Medicare National Coverage Determinations (NCD) Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;,&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Chapter 1, Part 3, Section 190.31 Prostate Specific Antigen&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Chapter 1, Part 4, Section 210.1 Prostate Cancer Screening Tests&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS IOM Publication 100-04, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual,&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Chapter 16 Laboratory Services&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS IOM Publication 100-08, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Program Integrity Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;,&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Chapter 13, Section 13.5.4 Reasonable and necessary Provision in an LCD&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt; background: white;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
