&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Italicized &lt;&sol;em&gt;font represents CMS national language&sol;wording copied directly from CMS Manuals or CMS Transmittals. Contractors are prohibited from changing national language&sol;wording.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(D) Investigational or Experimental&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IOM Citations:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CMS IOM Publication 100-08, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Program Integrity Manual,&lt;&sol;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;~ Chapter 13, 13.5.4 Reasonable and Necessary Provision in an LCD&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Social Security Act (Title XVIII) Standard References:&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, Section 1862(a)(1)(A) states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services which are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, Section 1862(a)(7). This section excludes routine physical examinations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code for Federal Regulations (CFR) References:&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CFR, Title 42, Ch. IV, &amp;sect;410.74 Physician assistant&#39;s services, &amp;sect;410.75 Nurse practitioner&#39;s services and &amp;sect;410.76 Clinical nurse specialist&#39;s services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
