indication:
&lt;p&gt;AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA using CCTA* is considered reasonable and medically necessary as a diagnostic study when:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient has acute or stable chest pain with no known CAD&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt; and is eligible for CCTA*, &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CCTA classifies patient as:&lt;br &sol;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate risk ** &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAD-RADS 1, CAD-RADS 2 or CAD-RADS 3 ***, category on CCTA&lt;sup&gt;1,2&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cardiac evaluation is&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;negative or inconclusive for acute coronary syndrome (ACS)&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;should not be performed until after the base study (CCTA) has been completed and interpreted. &amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Software to&lt;&sol;span&gt; perform AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA must be FDA cleared or approved.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;**Intermediate and high-risk as defined in the 2021 AHA&sol;ACC&sol;ASE&sol;CHEST&sol;SAEM&sol;SCCT&sol;SCMR Guideline for the Evaluation and Diagnosis of Chest Pain&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;*** &lt;&sol;span&gt;CAD-RADS 1-CAD-RADS 3 category as defined by CAD-RADS&amp;trade; 2.0&amp;ndash;2022 &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Coronary Artery Disease Reporting and Data System (CAD-RADS)&lt;&sol;span&gt;: an Expert Consensus document of the Society of Cardiovascular Computed Tomography (SCCT), the American College of Cardiology (ACC), the American College of Radiology (ACR), and the North America Society of Cardiovascular Imaging (NASCI).&lt;sup&gt;2,3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Limitations&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Software to perform AI-CPA must be FDA cleared or approved.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: none;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA is NOT considered reasonable or necessary in the following clinical circumstance (non-covered):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: none;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening, i.e., in the absence of signs, symptoms, or disease.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When there is a contraindication to CCTA.*&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with invasive coronary catheterization.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of normal CCTA results (CAD RADS=0 or no plaque disease).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of high grade stenosis (&amp;gt;70%) or CAD RADS-4 and RADS-5.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within 30 days of a myocardial infarction (MI).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of unstable coronary symptoms.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For disease surveillance.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Definitions&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Artificial Intelligence Enabled&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt; CT Based Quantitative Coronary Topography (&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;AI&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;-QCT&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt;)&sol;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Coronary Plaque Analysis&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt; (AI-CPA)- &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;artificial intelligence application to imaging obtained through coronary CT scans to calculate &lt;strong&gt;coronary artery dimensions and degree of stenosis per vessel and &lt;&sol;strong&gt;coronary plaque composition and burden. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Calcified Plaque&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;- &lt;&sol;span&gt;Higher density plaque, mostly composed of calcium, thought to be associated with lower clinical risk than non-calcified plaque. Traditionally, the overall burden of calcified plaque has been assessed indirectly through a coronary artery calcium score (CACS) or using cut off &amp;gt;350 HU.&lt;sup&gt;5 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;There is both calcified and non-calcified tissue present.&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coronary Artery Disease (CAD)- &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Narrowing of the coronary arteries usually caused by plaque and atherosclerosis that can lead to ischemia of the heart.&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Known CAD includes patient with prior anatomic testing with identified nonobstructive atherosclerotic plaque and obstructive CAD.&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Coronary Artery Disease Reporting and Data System (CAD-RADS)- &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;A standardized method to communicate findings of CCTA.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
