&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862 (a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those items or services that are considered to be medically reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;,&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &amp;sect;50.2 Determining Self-Administration of Drug or Biological and &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;&amp;sect;50.4.4.1 Antigens&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
