indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;This LCD addresses use of the fluid jet system treatment of lower urinary tract symptoms attributable to benign prostatic hyperplasia (LUTS&sol;BPH).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Indications&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Treatment for LUTS&sol;BPH will be considered reasonable and necessary when performed &lt;strong&gt;ONCE &lt;&sol;strong&gt;in patients with the following:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Indications including &lt;strong&gt;ALL&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the following:&lt;br &sol;&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;a&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Prostate volume of 30-150 cc&lt;sup&gt;1,2&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Persistent moderate to severe symptoms despite maximal medical management including &lt;strong&gt;ALL&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the following:
&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;i&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;International Prostate Symptom Score (IPSS) &amp;ge;12&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Maximum urinary flow rate (Qmax) of &amp;le;15 mL&sol;s&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Failure, contraindication or intolerance to at least three months of conventional medical therapy for LUTS&sol;BPH (e.g., alpha blocker, PDE5 Inhibitor, finasteride&sol;dutasteride)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Only treatment using an FDA approved&sol;cleared device will be considered reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Limitations&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following are considered not reasonable and necessary:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Body mass index &amp;ge; 42kg&sol;m2&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Known or suspected prostate cancer (based on NCCN Prostate Cancer Early Detection guidelines&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) or a prostate specific antigen (PSA) &amp;gt;&lt;u&gt;10&lt;&sol;u&gt; ng&sol;mL unless the patient has had a negative prostate biopsy within the last 6 months.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bladder cancer, neurogenic bladder, bladder calculus or clinically significant bladder diverticulum&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active urinary tract or systemic infection&lt;sup&gt;5&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment for chronic prostatitis&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnosis of urethral stricture, meatal stenosis, or bladder neck contracture&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Damaged external urinary sphincter&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Known allergy to device materials&lt;sup&gt;5&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inability to safely stop anticoagulants or antiplatelet agents preoperatively.&lt;sup&gt;5&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;This LCD supplements but does not replace, modify, or supersede existing Medicare applicable National Coverage Determinations (NCDs) or payment policy rules and regulations for cervical fusion procedures for pain management. Federal statute and subsequent Medicare regulations regarding provision and payment for medical services are lengthy. They are not repeated in this LCD. Neither Medicare payment policy rules nor this LCD replace, modify, or supersede applicable state statutes regarding medical practice or other health practice professions acts, de?nitions and scopes of practice. All providers who report services for Medicare payment must fully understand and follow all existing laws, regulations, and rules for Medicare payment for EPIDURAL procedures for pain management and must properly submit only valid claims for them. Please review and understand them and apply the medical necessity provisions in the policy within the context of the manual rules. Relevant CMS manual instructions and policies may be found in the following Internet-Only Manuals (IOMs) published on the CMS Web site:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.3pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IOM Citations:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;CMS IOM Publication 100-08, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Program Integrity Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, &lt;br &sol;&gt;~ Chapter 13, 13.5.4 Reasonable and Necessary Provision in an LCD&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Social Security Act (Title XVIII) Standard References:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, Section 1862(a)(1)(A) states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services which are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 11.6pt;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, Section 1862(a)(7). This section excludes routine physical examinations.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) References:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;CFR, Title 42, Ch. IV, &amp;sect; 410.74 Physician assistants&amp;rsquo; services, &amp;sect;410.75 Nurse practitioners&amp;rsquo; services and &amp;sect; 410.76 Clinical nurse specialists&amp;rsquo; services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.4pt;&quot;&gt;Compliance with the provisions in this LCD may be monitored and addressed through post payment data analysis and subsequent medical review audits.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;History&sol;Background and General Information&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Indications of Coverage&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A. Cervical fusion surgery is considered medically reasonable and necessary for the decompression of symptomatic cervical nerve root impingement when all of the following requirements are met:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Persistent or recurrent moderate or severe arm pain (4 or more on the visual analog scale or equivalent) present for a minimum of 12 weeks within the current episode of arm pain with documented failure to respond to multimodal conservative management (as tolerated) in the absence of exceptional circumstances (below) &lt;strong&gt;AND &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Nerve compression negatively impacts activities of daily living &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;All other potential sources of pain&sol;neurological deficit have been excluded &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Imaging (MRI or CT) evidence of central, lateral recess or foraminal stenosis at the level corresponding with clinical myotome signs or symptoms and including at least one of the following:
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cervical degenerative disc disease as indicated by the presence of one or more of the following findings: herniated nucleus pulposus, narrowing of the intervertebral disc, disc osteophytes, facet hypertrophy, or synovial cysts.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tumors (primary or metastatic)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post infection radiographic findings&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spinal instability as defined by subluxation or translation more than 3.5 mm on static lateral views or dynamic radiographs OR sagittal plane angulation of more than 11 degrees between adjacent segments.&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Limitations&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;The following is considered not reasonable and necessary for the decompression of symptomatic cervical nerve root impingement:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Isolated chronic axial cervical pain&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Exceptions to conservative therapy requirement for decompression of symptomatic cervical nerve root impingement:&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Concomitant myelopathy or myeloradiculopathy
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Cervical myelopathy class III or above&lt;strong&gt; OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Progression of neurological deficits during the trial of conservative treatment.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Isolated radiculopathy
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Presenting with progressive motor weakness &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Significant motor weakness interfering with ADLs &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Severe radicular pain defined as pain limiting ability to perform activities of daily living (AOLs) and &amp;ge;7&sol;10 on VAS or equivalent scale2 AND associated with confirmatory imaging (computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging) and clinical-radiological correlation&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loss of bladder or bowel function due to cervical spinal cord compression&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B. Cervical fusion surgery is considered reasonable and necessary for the decompression of symptomatic cervical canal stenosis when the following requirements are met:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;1. Persistent or recurrent moderate or severe arm pain (4 or more on the visual analog scale or equivalent) present for a minimum of 12 weeks within the episode of arm pain with documented failure to respond to multimodal conservative management (as tolerated) in the absence of exceptional circumstances (below) &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;2. Nerve compression negatively impacts activities of daily living &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;3. Spastic gait, loss of manual dexterity, problems with sphincter control &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;4. All other potential sources of pain&sol;neurological deficit have been excluded &lt;strong&gt;AND &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;5. Imaging (MRI or CT) evidence of central stenosis at the level corresponding with clinical signs or symptoms and including at least one of the following:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Cervical degenerative disc disease as indicated by the presence of one or more of the following findings: herniated nucleus pulposus, narrowing of the intervertebral disc, disc osteophytes, facet hypertrophy, or synovial cysts.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Congenital short pedicles&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tumors (primary or metastatic)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post infection radiographic findings&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ossification of the posterior longitudinal ligament.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spinal instability as defined by subluxation or translation more than 3.5 mm on static lateral views or dynamic radiographs OR sagittal plane angulation of more than 11 degrees between adjacent segments.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt; Cord compression with or without increased cord signal. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Limitations&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The following are considered not reasonable and necessary for &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;decompression of symptomatic cervical canal stenosis:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Isolated chronic axial cervical pain.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Asymptomatic myelopathy (regardless of severity on imaging findings).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Exceptions to conservative therapy requirement for decompression of symptomatic cervical canal stenosis:&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Myelopathy
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Cervical myelopathy class III or above &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Progression of neurological deficits during the trial of conservative treatment.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Radiculopathy
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Presenting with progressive motor weakness &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Significant motor weakness interfering with ADLs &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Severe radicular pain defined as pain limiting ability to perform activities of daily living (AOLs) and &amp;ge;7&sol;10 on Visual Analog Scale (VAS) or equivalent scale&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;&sol;sup&gt; AND associated with confirmatory imaging (computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging) and clinical-radiological correlation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loss of bladder or bowel function due to cervical spinal cord compression&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C. Cervical fusion surgery is considered reasonable and necessary for the decompression or stabilization of the cervical spine for the following indications: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;1. Traumatic injuries including fractures, dislocations, facture-dislocations, or traumatic ligamentous disruption when&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Fractures or dislocations which are likely to result spinal instability without neurological defects &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Fractures or dislocations associated with neurological defects at the affected level &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Instability is present.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;2. Spinal tumors involving the spine or spinal canal when:&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Malignant or benign tumors which have caused instability or neurologic deficit where treatment of the tumor will likely require stabilization of the spine.&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;&sol;sup&gt; &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Expected treatment of the tumor whether by chemotherapy or radiation therapy or surgery will likely cause spinal instability or neurologic deficits.&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;&sol;sup&gt; &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Instability is present.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;3.Infection involving the spine in the form of discitis, osteomyelitis, or epidural abscess when&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Imaging or other studies (MRI, biopsy, bone aspirate) demonstrating infection &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Imaging evidence of vertebral body destruction OR documentation that spinal debridement will cause vertebral instability&lt;sup&gt;5,6&lt;&sol;sup&gt; &lt;strong&gt;OR &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;Instability is present.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;4. Deformities that include the cervical spine including when&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cervical kyphosis associated with cord compression or Atlantoaxial (C1-C2) subluxation or Basilar invagination of the odontoid process into the foramen magnum; &lt;em&gt;or&lt;&sol;em&gt; Subaxial (C2-T1) instability kyphosis, head drop syndrome, post-laminectomy deformity OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Symptomatic pseudarthrosis (non-union of prior fusion) with radiological (e.g., CT or MRI) demonstration of non-union of prior fusion (lack of bridging bone or abnormal motion at fused segment) after 12 months since fusion surgery &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;or&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;with radiographic evidence of hardware failure (fracture or displacement). OR&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spinal instability after laminectomy &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: white;&quot;&gt;Rheumatoid arthritis with associated instability &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cervical degenerative spondylolisthesis with spinal instability (Anterolisthesis&sol;Posterolisthesis)&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;AND:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: circle;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial functional limitation is present such as severe neck pain, or difficulty ambulating, or decreased ability to perform ADLs or to maintain forward gaze. &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progression of deformity&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Limitations&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cervical Fusion for the decompression or stabilization of the cervical spine is not reasonable and necessary when all the above criteria are not fulfilled.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provider Qualifications&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Medicare Program Integrity Manual states services will be considered reasonable and necessary only if performed by appropriately trained providers.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Patient safety and quality of care mandate that healthcare professionals who perform cervical fusion are appropriately trained and credentialed by a formal residency&sol;fellowship program. Credentialing or privileges are required for procedures performed in inpatient and outpatient settings.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All aspects of care must be within the provider&amp;rsquo;s medical licensure and scope of practice. Reimbursement for procedures utilizing imaging techniques may be made to providers who meet training requirements for the procedures in this policy only if their respective state allows such in their practice act and formally licenses or certifies the practitioner to use and interpret these imaging modalities (ionizing radiation and associated contrast material, magnetic resonance imaging, ultrasound). At a minimum, training must cover and develop an understanding of anatomy and drug pharmacodynamics and kinetics as well as proficiency in diagnosis and management of disease, the technical performance of the procedure, and utilization of the required associated imaging modalities.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notice: &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Services performed for any given diagnosis must meet all the indications and limitations stated in this LCD, the general requirements for medical necessity as stated in CMS payment policy manuals, all existing CMS national coverage determinations, and all Medicare payment rules.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Definitions&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.55pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Acute Pain&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;an unpleasant sensory and emotional experience associated with actual or potential tissue damage which is present for up to 6 weeks.&lt;sup&gt;7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Baseline Pain- &lt;&sol;strong&gt;An initial measurement of the pain which is taken at a specified time point and used for comparison over time to look for changes in the pain levels.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cervical Radiculopathy-&lt;&sol;strong&gt; Pain in a radicular pattern in one or both upper extremities related to compression and irritation of one or more cervical nerve roots.&lt;sup&gt;8&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chronic Pain&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;The temporal definition of pain persisting at least 12 weeks after the onset of the acute pain.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conservative Therapy&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Consists of an appropriate combination of medication in therapeutic dosages (e.g., non-steroidal anti-inflammatory [NSAIDs], serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors (SNRIs), analgesics, etc.) administered for a sufficient amount of time to determine efficacy, in combination with either physical therapy, spinal manipulation therapy, cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT), home exercise program, acupuncture, or other interventions based on the individual&amp;rsquo;s specific presentation, physical findings, and imaging results.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consistent Improvement &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;The progressive, incremental, and clinically meaningful improvement of physical signs or symptoms.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 13.5pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disability&lt;&sol;strong&gt; &amp;ndash; Activity limitations or participation restrictions in an individual with a health condition, disorder or disease.&lt;sup&gt;9&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Impairment - &lt;&sol;strong&gt; A physical or functional or physiological impairment causing deviation from the normal function of a tissue or organ. This results in a significantly limited, impaired or delayed capacity to move, coordinate actions or perform physical activities and is exhibited by difficulties in one or more of the following areas: physical and motor tasks; independent movement; performing basic life functions.&lt;sup&gt;9&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRADE &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&amp;ndash; A system developed by the GRADE Working Group to address the shortcomings of present grading systems in healthcare. The GRADE system uses a common, sensible, and transparent approach to grading the quality of evidence. The results of applying the GRADE system to clinical trial data are displayed in a table known as a GRADE profile.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hangman&amp;rsquo;s Fracture &lt;&sol;strong&gt;- a bilateral fracture traversing the pars interarticularis of cervical vertebrae 2 (C2) with an associated traumatic subluxation of C2 on cervical vertebrae 3 (C3).&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multidisciplinary Biopsychosocial Rehabilitation (MBR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;)&lt;&sol;u&gt; &amp;ndash; Targets physical as well as psychological and social aspects of pain and involves a team of healthcare providers with different professional backgrounds and training.&lt;u&gt; &lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 14.15pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Myelopathy- &lt;&sol;strong&gt;An inclusive term describing a compression of the spinal cord resulting in neurological deficits e.g., spasticity (sustained muscle contractions), hyperreflexia, pathologic reflexes, paresthesia affecting the extremities, muscle weakness, digit&sol;hand clumsiness, or gait disturbance.&lt;sup&gt;11,12&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 11.55pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nonspecific low back pain&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;ndash; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Back pain that cannot be attributed to a specific disease or spinal pathology&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Session-&lt;&sol;strong&gt; A session is a time period, which includes all procedures (e.g., SIJIs and RFA ablations) that are performed during the same day.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustained and Constant Pain Relief&lt;&sol;strong&gt; - The pain relief must continue for the defined time period and without interruption or regression to the primary (index) pain.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Symptomatic pseudarthrosis&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;- (non-union of prior fusion) with radiological (e.g., CT or MRI) demonstration of non-union of prior fusion (lack of bridging bone or abnormal motion at fused segment) 12 months or more since fusion surgery &lt;em&gt;or&lt;&sol;em&gt; with radiographic evidence of hardware failure (fracture or displacement).&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;sup&gt;13&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Unstable Spine-&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;cervical spinal instability has been defined as destruction of either the anterior or posterior elements of the spine making them nonfunctional, more than 3.5 mm of displacement of one vertebra in relation to another or greater than 11 degrees of rotational difference between adjacent vertebrae.&lt;sup&gt;1,14&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contractor Advisory Meeting &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal; background: white;&quot;&gt;A Multi-MAC Contractor Advisory Committee (CAC) Meeting was hosted by Noridian and included&lt;strong&gt; &lt;&sol;strong&gt;Noridian Healthcare Solutions, CGS Administrators, National Government Services, Palmetto GBA, WPS Government Health Administrators, First Coast Service Options and Novitas Solutions on August 16, 2023. The transcript and audio for this meeting is posted on each MACs website. Feedback from the subject matter experts is included through the evidence summary.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manuals, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Beneficiary Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;This Medicare contractor will provide limited coverage for molecular diagnostic tests used in the evaluation and management of patients who have undergone solid organ transplantation. These tests can inform decision making along with standard clinical assessments in their evaluation of organ injury for active rejection (AR).&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;These tests may be ordered by qualified physicians considering the diagnosis of AR affiliated with a transplant center, helping to rule in or out this condition when assessing the need for or results of a diagnostic biopsy. They should be considered along with other clinical evaluations and results and may be particularly useful in patients with significant contraindications to invasive procedures.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Molecular diagnostic tests that assess a transplanted allograft for rejection status are covered when ALL of the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The test must provide information about at least one of the two following clinical status determinations:&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;AR status&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Cellular or Antibody-mediated rejection (ACR or AMR) status&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The intended use of the test must be:&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;To assist in the evaluation of adequacy of immunosuppression, wherein a non-invasive or minimally invasive test can be used in lieu of a tissue biopsy in a patient for whom information from a tissue biopsy would be used to make a management decision regarding immunosuppression, OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;As a rule-out test for AR in validated populations of patients with clinical suspicion of rejection with a non-invasive or minimally invasive test to make a clinical decision regarding obtaining a biopsy, OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;For further evaluation of allograft status for the probability of allograft rejection after a physician-assessed pretest, OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;To assess rejection status in patients that have received a biopsy, but the biopsy results are inconclusive or limited by insufficient material.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The test demonstrates analytical validity (AV), including an analytical and clinical validation for any given measured analytes, and has demonstrated equivalence or superiority for sensitivity or specificity (depending on intended use) of detecting allograft rejection to other already-accepted tests for the same intended use measuring the same or directly comparable analytes.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Clinical validity (CV) of any analytes (or expression profiles) measured must be established through a study published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population. The degree of validity must be similar or superior to established and covered tests (see associated coverage Articles). If conducted with concordance to tissue histologic evaluation the Banff Classification for renal allografts or other accepted criteria (if existing) for other organs must be used.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The test is being used in a patient who is part of the population in which the test was analytically validated and has demonstrated CV.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;For a given patient encounter, only one molecular test for assessing allograft status may be performed UNLESS a second test, meeting all the criteria established herein, is reasonable and necessary as an adjunct to the first test.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;For minimally or non-invasive tests, the benefit to risk profile of the molecular test is considered by the ordering clinician to be more favorable than the benefit to risk profile of a tissue biopsy, or a tissue biopsy cannot be obtained. For example, this may be the case if a biopsy is considered medically contraindicated in a patient.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The test successfully completes a Technical Assessment that will ensure that AV, CV, and clinical utility criteria set in this policy are met to establish the test as Reasonable and Necessary.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Covered tests with AV that is significantly below similar services may have coverage rescinded.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

