indication:
&lt;p&gt;This contractor will cover molecular diagnostic tests for use in the evaluation and management of beneficiaries suspected of having Hereditary Transthyretin Amyloidosis (hATTR) when all the following criteria are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient has a clinical diagnosis of ATTR; OR
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has cardiac features suggestive of ATTR-cardiomyopathy; AND
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is of African ancestry; OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a first-degree relative with a hATTR diagnosis; OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has at least 1 additional feature suggestive of hATTR according to expert consensus and society guidelines.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has progressive sensorimotor and&sol;or autonomic neuropathy; AND
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a first-degree relative with a hATTR diagnosis; OR&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has at least 1 additional features suggestive of hATTR according to expert consensus and society guidelines.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient has been offered counseling regarding the test and potential results.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The results of the test will be used to aid in treatment decisions.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test performed includes at least the minimum genetic content (genes or genetic variants) with definitive or well-established guidelines-based evidence required for clinical decision making for its intended use that can be reasonably detected by the test.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test does not include additional genetic content that is not properly validated, or of unclear clinical validity or utility such that it could reasonably or possibly be mis-utilized by the patient or treating physician and result in impaired patient outcomes.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A single variant may be tested if it is the only variant considered to be reasonable and necessary for a patient given that it is a known familial variant.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The test has successfully completed a technical assessment (TA) that ensures the test is reasonable and necessary as described above.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

