indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;This is a limited coverage policy for assays that detect biomarkers from circulating tumor cells (CTCs).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Criteria for Coverage &lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cancers with established biomarker testing, as recommended by society or national guidelines&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Assays that detect biomarkers from CTCs are covered when ALL of the following are met:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;patient has been diagnosed with cancer&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The specific cancer type has an associated biomarker &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The associated biomarker has already established clinical utility (CU) in the peer-reviewed published literature for the intended cancer type and for the specific indication in the intended patient population &lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The biomarker&amp;rsquo;s CU may include any of the following: it can be used to diagnose, risk-stratify, predict, or monitor response to therapy, as recommended by national or society guidelines (i.e., American Society of Clinical Oncology (ASCO), National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN))&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;At least 1 of the following criteria are met AND there is clear documentation of at least 1 of these in the medical record: &lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The patient&amp;rsquo;s cancer has not previously been tested for the specific biomarker, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The patient has newly metastatic cancer, and a metastatic lesion has not been tested for the specific biomarker, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The patient demonstrates signs of clinical, radiological or pathologic disease progression, &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;There is concern for resistance to treatment based on specific and well-established clinical indications&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Testing for the biomarker can be performed using CTCs&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The CTC-based biomarker test successfully completes a comprehensive Technical Assessment (TA) by Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) that will ensure that Analytical Validity (AV) (including an analytical and clinical validation), Clinical Validity (CV), and CU criteria are met to establish the test as Reasonable and Necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The clinical validation has demonstrated performance that is equivalent or superior to tissue-based testing or another already-accepted test for the same biomarker for the same intended use.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CV (for new analytes) must be established through studies published in the peer-reviewed literature for the intended use of the test in the intended population.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Tissue-based testing for the specific biomarker is infeasible (e.g., quantity not sufficient or invasive biopsy is medically contraindicated) &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt; will not provide sufficient information for subsequent medical management (e.g., in cases where human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2) overexpression is negative in a tissue biopsy but may be positive in the CTCs, due to tumor heterogeneity). There is clear documentation of at least 1 of these reasons for testing in the medical record.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;For a given patient encounter, only 1 test for assessing the biomarker may be performed UNLESS a second test, meeting all the criteria established herein, is reasonable and necessary as an adjunct to the first test.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Duplicate testing of the same biomarker (&lt;em&gt;from the same sample type and for the same clinical indication&lt;&sol;em&gt;) using different methodologies is not covered. For example, testing for androgen receptor splice variant 7 (AR-V7) from CTCs by messenger RNA (mRNA) as well as &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;immunohistochemistry&lt;&sol;span&gt; (IHC)-based methodologies, for the same clinical indication, will not be covered.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A), states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;This is a limited coverage policy for Genomic derived tests that assess risk in localized (non-metastatic) prostate cancer. The review is focused on&amp;nbsp;the Decipher&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Prostate Cancer Classifier Assay (identified as Decipher&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; to follow). The test is considered reasonable and necessary to help identify men with localized Prostate Cancer and a life expectancy of at least 10 years who are good candidates for active surveillance according to the most recent National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) guidelines.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Decipher&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; is covered for men with prostate cancer:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;With localized or biochemically recurrent adenocarcinoma of the prostate (i.e., no clinical evidence of metastasis) who have a life expectancy of greater than or equal to 10 years if they are a candidate for and are considering (or being considered for) at least 1 of the following:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: disc;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Conservative management and yet would be eligible for definitive therapy (radical prostatectomy (RP), radiation or brachytherapy), or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Radiation therapy and yet would be eligible for the addition of a brachytherapy boost, or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Radiation therapy and yet would be eligible for the addition of short-term androgen deprivation therapy (ADT), or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Radiation therapy with short-term ADT yet would be eligible for the use of long-term ADT, or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Radiation with standard ADT yet would be eligible for systemic therapy intensification using next generation androgen signaling inhibitors or chemotherapy, or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Observation post-prostatectomy yet would be eligible for the addition of post-operative adjuvant radiotherapy, or;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Salvage radiotherapy post-prostatectomy yet would be eligible for the addition of ADT.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;The following criteria must also be met for coverage:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;The assay is performed on formalin-fixed paraffin embedded (FFPE) prostate biopsy tissue with at least 0.5 mm of linear tumor diameter or FFPE tissue from a prostate resection specimen, and;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Result will be used to determine treatment according to established practice guidelines, and;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Patient has not received pelvic radiation or ADT prior to the biopsy or prostate resection specimen, and;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Patient is monitored for disease progression according to established standards of care.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Other genomic tests that demonstrate an equivalent analytical validity and clinical validity will be considered reasonable and necessary for the same indications. Analytical and clinical validity will be assessed as part of a thorough and comprehensive technical assessment (TA) by the Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;)&amp;nbsp;and will similarly attain coverage for indications that are supported by the evidence and intended use within the scope of this policy.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

