indication:
&lt;p&gt;AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA using CCTA* is considered reasonable and medically necessary as a diagnostic study when:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patient has acute or stable chest pain with no known coronary artery disease (CAD)&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt; and is eligible for CCTA*, &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CCTA classifies patient as:&lt;br &sol;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate risk ** &lt;strong&gt;OR&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAD-RADS 1, CAD-RADS 2, or CAD-RADS 3*** category on CCTA &lt;sup&gt;1,2&lt;&sol;sup&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;AND&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cardiac evaluation is negative or inconclusive for acute coronary syndrome (ACS)&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*See L35121 for criteria for CCTA. AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA should not be performed until after the base study (CCTA) has been completed and interpreted. Software to perform AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA must be FDA cleared or approved.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**Intermediate and high-risk as defined in the 2021 AHA&sol;ACC&sol;ASE&sol;CHEST&sol;SAEM&sol;SCCT&sol;SCMR Guideline for the Evaluation and Diagnosis of Chest Pain&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*** CAD-RADS 1- CAD-RADS 3 category as defined by CAD-RADS&amp;trade; 2.0&amp;ndash;2022 Coronary Artery Disease Reporting and Data System (CAD-RADS): an Expert Consensus document of the Society of Cardiovascular Computed Tomography (SCCT), the American College of Cardiology (ACC), the American College of Radiology (ACR), and the North America Society of Cardiovascular Imaging (NASCI).&lt;sup&gt;2,3&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Limitations&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Software to perform AI-CPA must be FDA cleared or approved.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI-QCT&sol;AI-CPA is NOT considered reasonable or necessary in the following clinical circumstance (non-covered):&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening, i.e., in the absence of signs, symptoms, or disease.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When there is a contraindication to CCTA*&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with invasive coronary catheterization&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of normal CCTA results (CAD RADS=0 or no plaque disease)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of high grade stenosis (&amp;gt;70%) or CAD RADS-4 and RADS-5&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within 30 days of a myocardial infarction (MI).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the presence of unstable coronary symptoms&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For disease surveillance&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*See CCTA policy (L35121) for full listing of contraindications.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Definitions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artificial Intelligence Enabled CT Based Quantitative Coronary Topography (AI-QCT)&sol;Coronary Plaque Analysis (AI-CPA)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;- Artificial intelligence application to imaging obtained through coronary CT scans to calculate coronary artery dimensions and degree of stenosis per vessel and coronary plaque composition and burden.&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calcified Plaque&lt;&sol;strong&gt;- Higher density plaque, mostly composed of calcium, thought to be associated with lower clinical risk than non-calcified plaque. Traditionally, the overall burden of calcified plaque has been assessed indirectly through a coronary artery calcium score (CACS) or using cut off &amp;gt;350 HU.&lt;sup&gt;5&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;There is both calcified and non-calcified tissue present&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;&sol;sup&gt;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coronary Artery Disease (CAD)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;- Narrowing of the coronary arteries usually caused by plaque and atherosclerosis that can lead to ischemia of the heart.&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Known CAD includes patient with prior anatomic testing with identified nonobstructive atherosclerotic plaque and obstructive CAD.&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coronary Artery Disease Reporting and Data System (CAD-RADS)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;- A standardized method to communicate findings of CCTA.&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
