indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Transanal endoscopic surgery (TES) may be considered medically necessary for treatment of rectal adenomas, including recurrent adenomas that cannot be removed using other means of local excision.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;TES may be considered medically necessary for treatment of clinical stage T1 rectal adenocarcinomas that cannot be removed using other means of local excision and that meet &lt;u&gt;all&lt;&sol;u&gt; of the following criteria:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Located within 8 cm of the anal verge&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Less than 3 cm in size&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Well-to-moderately differentiated (G1 or G2) by biopsy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Without lymphadenopathy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Less than 30% of the circumference of the rectum&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;TES may be considered medically necessary for treatment of rectal carcinoid tumors that cannot be removed using other means of local excision and that meet all of the following criteria:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Located within 8 cm of the anal verge&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Less than 2 cm in size&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;No radiologic evidence of metastasis&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Less than 30% of the circumference of the rectum&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;TES is considered investigational for treatment of rectal tumors that do not meet the criteria noted.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Credentialing and Accreditation Standards&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Optimal outcomes of TES procedures depend on the knowledge, skill and experience of the provider. Services will be considered medically reasonable and necessary only if performed by appropriately trained providers.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FDA Indications&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.accessdata.fda.gov&sol;scripts&sol;cdrh&sol;cfdocs&sol;cfpmn&sol;pmn.cfm?ID=K000180&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Transanal Endoscopic microsurgery (TEM) combination system and instrument set. 510K Summary: K000180.&lt;&sol;a&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.accessdata.fda.gov&sol;scripts&sol;cdrh&sol;cfdocs&sol;cfpmn&sol;pmn.cfm?ID=K133393&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;GelPOINT Path Transanal Access Platform. 510K Summary: K133393&lt;&sol;a&gt;.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
