cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A), states that no Medicare payment shall be made for items or services that are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(a) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;80 Requirements for Diagnostic X-Ray, Diagnostic Laboratory, and Other Diagnostic Tests, &amp;sect;80.1.1 Certification Changes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;National Coverage Determination (NCD) 90.2, which allows contractors to cover next generation sequencing tests as a diagnostic laboratory test for patients with cancer in specific circumstances&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This policy describes and clarifies coverage for Lab-Developed Tests (LDTs), Federal Drug Administration (FDA)-cleared, and FDA-approved clinical laboratory tests in hereditary cancer tests including Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) tests as allowable under the National Coverage Determination (NCD) 90.2, under section D describing Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) discretion for coverage. This policy&amp;rsquo;s scope is specific for hereditary germline testing, and is exclusive of polygenic risk scores, solid tumor, hematologic malignancies, circulating tumor &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;deoxyribonucleic acid (&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;DNA) testing (ctDNA), and other acquired cancer-related tests.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt;Criteria for Coverage&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;All the following must be present for coverage eligibility:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; The patient must have:&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Any cancer diagnosis&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;AND a clinical indication for germline (inherited) testing for hereditary cancer&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;AND a risk factor for germline (inherited) cancer &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;AND has not been previously tested for the same germline genetic content.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test has satisfactorily completed a Technical Assessment (TA) by Molecular Diagnostic Services Program (MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt;) for the stated indications of the test.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test performed includes &lt;strong&gt;at least&lt;&sol;strong&gt; the minimum genetic content (genes or genetic variants) with definitive or well-established guidelines-based evidence required for clinical decision making for its intended use that can be reasonably detected by the test.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Because these genes and variants will change as the literature and drug indications evolve, they are listed separately in associated documents, such as the MolDX&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; TA forms. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A single gene or variant may be tested if it is the only gene or variant considered to be reasonable and necessary for a cancer type. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;If a previous&amp;nbsp;test was performed with a similar&sol;duplicative intended use, a subsequent test is only reasonable and necessary if the non-duplicative genetic content of the second test is reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;If the test is an NGS test, it must abide by all conditions listed in the NCD 90.2.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Situations in which a test should not be used or coverage is denied:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The test in question will be non-covered if:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;It is an NGS test and does not fulfill all the criteria set forth in the NCD 90.2&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A previous test was performed for the same genetic content&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;It is a panel or single gene test used to identify a known familial variant(s) that could be identified with a test targeted to that specific variant(s)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;It is a panel or single gene test used to confirm a variant(s) detected by somatic tumor testing that can be confirmed by a test targeted to that specific variant(s)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A satisfactory TA is not completed&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For tests that are currently covered but a TA submission has not been made, providers must submit complete TA materials by the original effective date of the policy or coverage will be denied.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) excludes expenses incurred for items or services which are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA), &amp;sect;1862(a)(7) excludes routine physical examinations.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-03, Medicare National Coverage Determinations (NCD) Manual, Chapter 1, Part 4, &amp;sect;220.1 Computed Tomography (CT)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;CTP (using automated post-processing software algorithmic analysis) is medically reasonable and necessary in patients with acute ischemic stroke (AIS) caused by unilateral large vessel occlusion (LVO) in the proximal anterior circulation evaluated at stroke centers; CTP can be used to aid in selection for endovascular mechanical thrombectomy (EVT) if the following other conditions are fulfilled:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: decimal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: normal; background: white;&quot;&gt;NIH score &amp;ge; 6&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 105%;&quot;&gt;EVT treatment (femoral puncture) can be started within &lt;strong&gt;6-24 hours&lt;&sol;strong&gt; of the time last known to be at neurologic baseline&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The pre-stroke baseline mRS&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;&sol;span&gt; 2 (slight to no disability)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 106%;&quot;&gt;Stroke is the leading cause of adult disability in the United States (U.S.) with limited treatment options.&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt; The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved treatment for stroke is intravenous (IV) tissue plasminogen activator (tPA)within 3 hours after onset of symptoms. Often treatment is not initiated since most patients do not present within this narrow time window, resulting in only 4% of patients receiving tPA treatment. Even with treatment, only 12-25% benefit as irreversible injury may have already occurred, or the treatment fails to recanalize the occluded artery with reported recanalization rate of 10-50%.&lt;sup&gt;2,4&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Endovascular stroke therapy involves mechanical removal of blood clots or intra-arterial administration of thrombolytics. This offers an alternative to patients who fail tPA or are not eligible. Recanalization rates are as high as 82% for thrombectomy.&lt;sup&gt;5&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Initial studies on EVT failed to demonstrate clinical benefits.&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Further investigation suggested the lack of benefit was related to patient selection. Subsequent studies identified imaging criteria to determine patients with potentially salvageable tissues and improved outcomes from EVT.&lt;sup&gt;6-8 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;In stroke victims, there is the ischemic penumbra, potentially salvageable tissue, and ischemic core, which is irreversibly injured. Patients with &amp;gt;50% reperfusion have been shown to have an improved outcome compared to those with &amp;lt;50% reperfusion. Treatment of patients with a higher likelihood of improved outcomes demonstrates the benefit of EVT in select patients. Expansion of the treatment window up to 16-24 hours has promising results in appropriately selected patients expanding the possibility for acute stroke treatment.&lt;sup&gt;2,9&lt;&sol;sup&gt; CTP plays a role, as it can be used to calculate the ischemic penumbra and help to identify which patients may benefit from EVT. Reperfusion treatment was found to be more common in patients who had imaging with &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CT angiography &lt;&sol;span&gt;(CTA) (13%) or CTP (17.6%).&lt;sup&gt;10 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Noncontrast CT (NCCT) is the mainstay for initial AIS imaging due to widespread availability, rapid scan times, and detection of intracranial hemorrhage (which leads to very different &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;management from infarction). Multimodal CT includes &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;NCCT, CTA (to assess the site of vascular occlusion), and CTP imaging. CTP is typically performed after NCCT and consists of a temporal sequence of head &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;CT scans obtained during the wash-in and wash-out of an IV bolus of iodinated contrast agent. Post-acquisition data analysis by dedicated software allows the creation of multiple &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;hemodynamic parametric maps (based on contrast time-density curves) for clinical interpretation. Hemodynamic parameters include time to maximum contrast intensity (Tmax), mean &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;transit time (MTT), cerebral blood flow (CBF), and cerebral blood volume (CBV), mathematically related by the equation CBF = CBV&sol;MTT.&lt;sup&gt;11&lt;&sol;sup&gt; The CBV is calculated as the millimeters of blood &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;per 100g of brain tissue. These maps can estimate brain regions with a high probability of irreversible &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;infarction (ischemic core) versus areas of potentially reversible ischemia (penumbra). &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Both core and penumbra are estimates of probabilistic tissue fate. Penumbra imaging has been proposed as a useful predictor of hemorrhagic transformation (HT) in AIS.&lt;sup&gt;12 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;HT occurs in up &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;to 40% of stroke patients and is related to rapid deterioration and poor outcomes. CTP has been studied in AIS for decades,&lt;sup&gt;13&lt;&sol;sup&gt; only recently was it found likely to influence &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;treatment decision.&lt;sup&gt;14&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Subsequently, 2 level I randomized controlled trials (RCTs) (DAWN and DEFUSE 3) found CTP helped determine eligibility for EVT in the late time period (6-24 hr) of &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;an AIS (&amp;lt;24 hr),&lt;sup&gt;2,9&lt;&sol;sup&gt; a paradigm shift away from confinement to the early window (&amp;lt; 6 hr)&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;CTP has the advantage of being able to be performed by most multi-slice scanners and add minimal time, usually less than 10 minutes, to the evaluation. There are limitations to CTP&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; technology, emphasizing that CTP must be performed in properly selected patients. There are potential technical issues, such as patient movement and poor contrast bolus that can impact &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;results. While experienced providers can typically recognize abnormalities caused by artifacts, calculations provided by the software may include artifacts, risking overestimating the &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;penumbral volume. This requires manual correction to avoid miscalculations. Another challenge is there are multiple CTP vendor software and postprocessing techniques, which may lead to variations in calculated core and mismatch.&lt;sup&gt;11,15&lt;&sol;sup&gt; Ideally, the software programs would be standardized, but given the variability, providers must be familiar with the software package being &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;used and potential variations in calculated values. Automation has the potential to reduce human variability; however, even with fully automated software, a significant clinician &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;interpretation learning curve remains.&lt;sup&gt;16 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;Limitations of arterial flow, which can be caused by low cardiac output, arrhythmias, chronic carotid stenosis, may result in overestimations. Chronic &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;infarction, vascular stenosis, chronic white matter changes, seizures, and vasospasm can demonstrate abnormal CTP patterns and potentially mimic acute ischemia, so the provider must consider the full medical picture when interpreting results.&lt;sup&gt;11,17 &lt;&sol;sup&gt;CTP requires contrast, so those with renal failure or known serious allergy to iodine and previously refractory to pretreatment &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;medications may not be candidates. Protocols should include care to avoid excess radiation exposure and avoid treatment delays. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;; font-size: 10.5pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Verdana;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in 0in 0pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;; font-size: 10.5pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Verdana;&quot;&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(D) research and experimental must be reasonable and necessary.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in 0in 0pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in 0in 0pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;This Local Coverage Determination (LCD) addresses use of &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.accessdata.fda.gov&sol;cdrh_docs&sol;pdf15&sol;P150038S006B.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Magnetic Resonance Guided Focused Ultrasound Surgery System (MRgFUS)&lt;&sol;a&gt; for the treatment of neurologic conditions.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;MRgFUS unilateral thalamotomy is considered medically reasonable and necessary in patients who have essential tremor (ET) and all of the following:&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Medication refractory ET (defined as refractory to at least 2 trials of medical therapy, including at least 1 first-line agent)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Moderate to severe postural or intention tremor of the dominant hand (defined by a score of &amp;ge;2 on the Clinical Rating Scale for Tremor (CRST))&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Disabling ET (defined by a score of &amp;ge;2 on any of the 8 items in the disability subsection of the CRST)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Has failed deep brain stimulation (DBS) or is not able to tolerate the procedure due to other medical problems&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;MRgFUS unilateral thalamotomy is considered medically reasonable and necessary in patients who have Tremor-Dominant Parkinson&amp;rsquo;s disease (TDPD) and all of the following:&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Medication refractory TDPD, defined as refractory (or intolerant) to levodopa or levodopa equivalent medications (LEDD) &amp;ge; 900 mg&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Parkinson&amp;rsquo;s disease (PD) with tremor-dominant subtype. This should generally be reflected by administering the unified Parkinson&#39;s disease rating scale (UPDRS) in the on-medication state using the ratio of the mean score for tremor items (items 16, 20, and 21) to the mean postural instability&sol;gait disorder score (items 13-15,29, and 30). A ratio of &amp;ge; 1.5 indicates TDPD&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Severe and disabling tremor as indicated by documentation of specific activities in daily life that the patient is unable to perform or has substantial difficulty performing secondary to the tremor&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Has failed DBS or is not able to tolerate the procedure due to other medical problems&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Limitations (not covered):&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Treatment of head or voice tremor&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Bilateral thalamotomy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Conditions
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Unstable cardiac disease&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Coagulopathy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Risk factors for deep-vein thrombosis&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Severe depression (defined by a score &amp;ge;20 on Patient Health Questionnaire 9 (PHQ-9))&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Cognitive impairment (defined by a score of &amp;lt;24 on the Mini&amp;ndash;Mental State Examination)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Previous brain procedure (transcranial magnetic stimulation, DBS, stereotactic lesioning, or electroconvulsive therapy)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;A skull density ratio (the ratio of cortical to cancellous bone) &amp;lt;0.40&lt;sup&gt;11,12&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 14.4pt;&quot;&gt;Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) contraindicated&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

