indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This is a coverage policy for Advance Care Planning.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Voluntary&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; Advance Care Planning (ACP) is a face-to-face service between a physician or other qualified healthcare professional (QHP) and a patient and&sol;or family member and&sol;or surrogate to discuss the patient&amp;rsquo;s healthcare wishes if he&sol;she should become unable to make decisions about their own care.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;ACP can be offered as either:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;An optional element of a Medical Wellness Visit:&amp;nbsp; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Per the Annual Wellness Visit (AWV)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;; or per&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A separate Medicare Part B medically necessary service&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The primary goal of ACP is to facilitate people receiving medical care that is consistent with their personal values, goals and preferences.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Excellent examples of ACP services may include, but are not limited to the following content:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Introducing and discussing the value and importance of basic ACP;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Exploring current and past experiences of loved ones who have been seriously ill or have died;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Exploring goals of care in the event of sudden injury or illness;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Exploring goals of care when there would be little chance for patients to recover or to have the ability to know who they are or who they are with;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Identifying and&sol;or preparing a healthcare agent;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Completing or updating an advance directive document (not required); and &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Transferring patients&amp;rsquo; preferences into actionable medical orders.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;ACP codes describe counseling and discussion of advance care directives with the patient, family members, and&sol;or surrogate. Such services may or may not include completion of pertinent legal documents. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;An advance directive is described as a written document that a patient uses to appoint a representative and&sol;or to record his or her wishes as they relate to future medical treatment in the event the patient is incapacitated and unable to make decisions on his or her own. Types of written advance directives include, but are not limited to:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Healthcare proxy&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Durable power of attorney for healthcare&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Living will&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Medical orders for life-sustaining treatment (MOLST)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Such formal written documents are not required, but may be included, in the provision of ACP services.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The physician&sol;QHP providing ACP services must assess patients&amp;rsquo; decision-making capacity before deeming them unable to speak for themselves. Decision-making capacity is task-specific. In other words, a disease&sol;condition may prevent a patient from accomplishing certain tasks, but not affect abilities to express advance care desires. Conversely, patients who appear superficially intact may not be able to comprehend the nuanced details or pros&sol;cons of upcoming medical care. Determinations of decisional capacity for ACP require neither legal intervention nor psychiatric expertise. There is no singular test of decision-making capacity. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Again, ACP service provision requires the permission of the patient or, in the absence of sufficient decision-making capacity, the family member or surrogate. The offer of voluntary participation and the acceptance of ACP should be documented.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;ACP services are time based. No other active management of the patient&amp;rsquo;s problems should be undertaken for the time period reported when ACP codes are used. Brief conversations of just a few minutes (done in the course of an E&sol;M service) related to wishes concerning potential emergent resuscitation do not represent ACP services.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Professional services are those face-to-face services rendered by physicians and other qualified health care professionals who may report E&sol;M services by a specific CPT&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;&sol;sup&gt; code. Face-to-face time is defined as only that time spent face-to-face with the patient and&sol;or family. This includes the time spent performing such tasks as:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Obtaining a history&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Examination&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Counseling the patient&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;In order to support the requirements necessary to verify that face-to-face services occurred, clear and concise medical record documentation is critical. The nature and amount of physician&sol;QHP work required, type of service, place of service and the patient status should be evident on medical record review. Accordingly, telephone audio-only conversations with family members or surrogates should not be included in face-to-face time calculations for ACP services. If ACP services are offered via telehealth, the specific CMS guidelines for telehealth, in effect at the time of such services, would be applied.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,sans-serif;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;There is no limit on the number of times ACP can be reported for a beneficiary in a given time period. However, if this service is billed more than once, it is expected that a &lt;em&gt;change&lt;&sol;em&gt; in the patient&amp;rsquo;s health status and&sol;or wishes about end-of-life care would be clearly documented.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Should records be requested for review of multiple ACP claims, documentation would be expected to support the reasonable and necessary use of ACP as evidenced by the following:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The content and the medical necessity of the ACP related discussion;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Voluntary participation in ACP by the patient, or in the case of absent decision-making capacity, by the family member or surrogate;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;A change in health status or advance care wishes in order to support repetitive provision of ACP services;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The scenario for the service: face to face, by phone, as a telehealth service including audio and&sol;or video communication;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The time spent solely for provision of ACP services; and&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The names of participants involved in the discussion&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

cms_cov_policy:
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;411.15(a) and (k) Particular services excluded from coverage.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 6, &amp;sect;20.5.1 Coverage of Outpatient Therapeutic Services Incident to a Physician&amp;rsquo;s Service Furnished on or After August 1, 2000, and Before January 1, 2010.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 8, &amp;sect;50.5 Drugs and Biologicals.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 13, &amp;sect;110 Physician Services and &amp;sect;120 Services and Supplies Furnished &amp;ldquo;Incident to&amp;rdquo; Physician&amp;rsquo;s Services.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 15, &amp;sect;50 Drugs and Biologicals, &amp;sect;50.1 Definition of Drug or Biological, &amp;sect;50.2 Determining Self-Administration of Drug or Biological, &amp;sect;50.3 Incident To Requirements, &amp;sect;50.4.1 Approved Use of Drug, &amp;sect;50.4.2 Unlabeled Use of Drug, &amp;sect;50.4.3 Examples of Not Reasonable and Necessary, &amp;sect;50.4.5 Off-Label Use of Drugs and Biologicals in an Anti-Cancer Chemotherapeutic Regimen, &amp;sect;50.4.6 Less Than Effective Drug, and &amp;sect;200 Nurse Practitioner (NP) Services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-03, Medicare National Coverage Determinations (NCD) Manual, Chapter 1, Part 4, &amp;sect;250.3 Intravenous Immune Globulin for the Treatment of Autoimmune Mucocutaneous Blistering Diseases.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.fda.gov&sol;vaccines-blood-biologics&sol;approved-blood-products&sol;immune-globulins&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Intravenous Immune Globulin (IVIG)&lt;&sol;a&gt; is a solution of human immunoglobulins specifically prepared for intravenous infusion. Immunoglobulins contain a broad range of antibodies that act specifically against bacterial and viral antigens.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; INDICATIONS:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of primary immunodeficiency syndromes associated with defects in humoral immunity to replace or boost immunoglobulin G (IgG)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura (ITP) when a rapid rise in the platelet count is required such as prior to surgery, to control excessive bleeding, or to defer or avoid splenectomy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of Kawasaki disease, in conjunction with aspirin&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prevention of recurrent bacterial infections in patients with hypogammaglobulinemia associated with B-cell chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decreasing risk of acute graft versus host disease, associated interstitial pneumonia, and infections after bone marrow transplant in the first 100 days after transplantation&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reducing the risk of severe bacterial infections in human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infected children with a CD4 count of greater than 200 to 400&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Second-line treatment of certain autoimmune myopathies&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of adults with Guillain-Barr&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&amp;eacute;&lt;&sol;span&gt; syndrome diagnosed within the first 2 weeks of illness&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of hyperimmunoglobulinemia E syndrome and Lambert-Eaton myasthenic syndrome (LEMS)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of multifocal motor neuropathy (MMN)&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of chronic parvovirus B19 infection and severe anemia associated with bone marrow suppression and pure red cell aplasia&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of progressive pemphigus vulgaris, pemphigus foliaceus, bullous pemphigoid, mucous membrane pemphigoid, and epidermolysis bullosa acquisita in patients that have failed conventional treatment and patients in whom conventional therapy is otherwise contraindicated&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For coverage criteria of autoimmune mucocutaneous blistering diseases, please see CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-03, Medicare National Coverage Determinations Manual, Chapter 1, Part 4, &amp;sect;250.3&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of stiff person syndrome&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of myasthenia gravis (MG) in patients who have profound, rapidly progressive and&sol;or potentially life-threatening muscular weakness and are refractory to, or intolerant of cholinesterase inhibitors, corticosteroids and azathioprine&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prevention and&sol;or treatment of organ rejection in patients sensitized to living or cadaveric organ donors&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schonlein-Henoch&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of paraneoplastic visual loss&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy (CIDP) in patients meeting the necessary criteria&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treatment of multiple myeloma for the prevention of life-threatening infections due to reduced gamma globulins&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

