&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1812(a)(4) states in lieu of certain other benefits, hospice care with respect to the which the individual makes an election.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1812(d)(1) states payment under this part may be made for hospice care provided with respect to an individual only during 2 periods of 90 days each and an unlimited number of subsequent periods of 60 days each during the individual&amp;rsquo;s lifetime and only, with respect to each such period, if the individual makes an election under this paragraph to receive hospice care under this part provided by, or under arrangements made by, a particular hospice program instead of certain other benefits under this title.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1813(a)(4) addresses drugs and biologicals provided in a hospice program.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1814(a)(7) addresses certifying the patient for hospice.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1861(dd) states the term &quot;hospice care&quot; means the services provided to a terminally ill individual.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(9) addresses expenses for custodial care (except, in the case of hospice care, as is otherwise permitted).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
