indication:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Stem cell&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; transplantation is a process in which s&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;tem cells&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; are harvested from either a patient&amp;rsquo;s (autologous) or donor&amp;rsquo;s (allogeneic) bone marrow or peripheral blood for intravenous infusion. Autologous &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;s&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;tem cell&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; transplantation (AuSCT) is a technique for restoring stem &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;cell&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;s using the patient&#39;s own previously stored cells. AuSCT must be used to effect hematopoietic reconstitution following severely myelotoxic doses of chemotherapy (HDCT) and&sol;or radiotherapy used to treat various malignancies.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (allo-HSCT) is a procedure in which a portion of a healthy donor&#39;s stem cells or bone marrow is obtained and prepared for intravenous infusion. Hematopoietic stem cells are multi-potent cells that give rise to all the blood cell types; these stem cells form blood and immune cells. A hematopoietic stem cell is a cell isolated from blood or bone marrow that can renew itself, differentiate to a variety of specialized cells, can mobilize out of the bone marrow into circulating blood, and can undergo programmed cell death, called apoptosis - a process by which cells that are unneeded or detrimental will self-destruct.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;The Centers for Medicare &amp;amp; Medicaid Services (CMS) has clarified that bone marrow and peripheral blood stem cell transplantation is a process which includes mobilization, harvesting, and transplant of bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cells and the administration of high dose chemotherapy or radiotherapy prior to the actual transplant. When bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cell transplantation is covered, all necessary steps are included in coverage.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;NCD 110.23 Stem Cell Transplantation covers allo-HSCT for the following conditions, when reasonable and necessary: &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Leukemia&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Aplastic Anemia &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Severe Combined Immunodeficiency disease (SCID)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Wiskott-Aldrich Syndrome &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Allo-HSCT&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; is covered for Medicare beneficiaries with the following indications only when participating in approved prospective clinical studies meeting specific criteria under the Coverage with Evidence Development (CED) paradigm:&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Myelodysplastic Syndromes&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Multiple myeloma with Durie-Salmon Stage II or III disease, or International Staging System (ISS) Stage II or Stage III disease &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Myelofibrosis (MF) with Dynamic International Prognostic Scoring System (DIPSSplus) intermediate-2 or High primary or secondary disease; or&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Sickle cell disease (SCD) that is severe and symptomatic&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;(Please refer to CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-03, Medicare National Coverage Determinations Manual&lt;em&gt;,&lt;&sol;em&gt; Chapter 1, Part 2, &amp;sect;110.23 Stem Cell Transplantation)&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Per the NCD, &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;all other indications for &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;s&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;tem&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; c&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;ell&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;transplantation not otherwise noted as covered or non-covered remain at local Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) discretion.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%; background: white;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;This policy describes additional locally covered indications for allo-HSCT for primary refractory or relapsed Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphomas with B-cell or T-cell origin that are medically necessary in patients for whom there are no other curative intent options.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Documentation to support the reasonable and necessary nature of allo-HSCTs must speak to the serious illness of the patient, the reasons why the patient is considered to have relapsed or refractory disease, relevant clinical contextual information such as age, frailty, performance status, cardiopulmonary function, any associated organ dysfunction that could impact complications or recovery, screening for infectious diseases that could impact transplant care, nutritional status and patient specific psychosocial and financial support structures. Risk assessment scoring, such as the European Society for Blood and Bone Marrow Transplantation (EBMT) or the HCT Comorbidity Index (HCT-CI), should be strongly considered and in the case of any nationally covered indications per NCD 110.23 would of course be required.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

