&lt;p&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act, &amp;sect;1862(a)(1)(A) allows coverage and payment for only those services that are considered to be reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;410.32(b) Diagnostic x-ray tests, diagnostic laboratory tests, and other diagnostic tests: Conditions&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;42 CFR &amp;sect;411.15(k)(1) Particular services excluded from coverage&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;CMS Internet-Only Manual, Pub. 100-01, Medicare General Information, Eligibility and Entitlement Manual, Chapter 1, &amp;sect;10.3 Supplementary Medical Insurance (Part B) - A Brief Description&lt;&sol;p&gt;
